# The shape beside defect 088 (panel 177's brief, `use_after_consume`): the
# dead handle reaches a CONSUMING position. This one was already stopped
# before C, by the live set's stray report, since the address had left the set
# at the first delete. What changes under panel 177's item 1 is the SENTENCE:
# the crossing is asked first, so a handle whose own binding was emptied is
# named as dead rather than as a stray, and the reader is sent to the release
# that came too early rather than to a list of three causes.
#
# The ending call sits under an `if` on a value C returns, so the checker's
# half (item 3) lets the program reach the runtime.

extern "dead-handle-at-a-consuming-position-after-its-life-ended.h"
    record Json tag Obj
    function obj_new() -> Json acquires obj_delete
    function obj_add(object: Json, string: cstr lent, item: Json consumes) -> i64
    function obj_delete(item: Json consumes)
    function one() -> i64

function main()
    a = obj_new()
    b = obj_new()

    if one() == 1
        obj_delete(item: b)
    _ = obj_add(object: a, string: "b".cstr(), item: b)
    obj_delete(item: a)
